Euler form E = [[-1, -1], [0, -1]]
Serre operator S = E^-1 E^T = [[0, -1], [1, 1]]
char poly of S: lam**2 - lam + 1
  equals the sixth cyclotomic polynomial: True
  eigenvalues: [1/2 - sqrt(3)*I/2, 1/2 + sqrt(3)*I/2]
  in exponential form: exp(+- i pi/3), the two primitive sixth roots
S^3 = [[-1, 0], [0, -1]]  -> equals -I: True
S^6 = [[1, 0], [0, 1]]  -> equals  I: True

basis-free version: rank 2, integral, S^3 = -I, tr S = 1
  roots of lam^3 + 1:  {-1: 1, 1/2 - sqrt(3)*I/2: 1, 1/2 + sqrt(3)*I/2: 1}
  lam = -1 excluded by the trace, so the pair is exp(+- i pi/3);
  hence the primitive-sixth multiplicity is 2, which is nu_6 of the
  cubic threefold as computed in the manuscript from Cai's connection.

ambient contrast: S_X = (tensor omega)[3] acts on K_num as -1 times a
unipotent (tensoring by a line bundle is unipotent on the Chern
character), so every ambient eigenvalue is -1 and none is a primitive
sixth root.  The count is a residual-component invariant.
